che part <num> was a fascinating experiment which did not only tell a very interesting story but it also tried to do something different with the biopic genre.che part <num> is the excellent culmination of this experiment   this movie offers all of the same attributes from the <num> <num> from the extraordinary performances specially from benicio del toro to steven soderbergh 's brilliant direction without forgetting its intention of breaking with the conventional rules from the biopics.that is what i admire from soderbergh 's experiments they always try to do something different and unusual and they succeed most of the times   the final message from this film is perfect and it includes everything we have been told about che guervara 's life.the only fail i found on che part <num> is that a few parts felt a bit irrelevant   in summary i give che part <num> a very enthusiastic recommendation because as the <num> <num> it is a brave and fascinating experiment which challenges the spectator and leaves us thinking 

