the story for the <num> aired television installment of columbo is simple <num> half of successful mystery writing team does away with the other frames an unseen mafia group is blackmailed by an admirer does away with the admirer and is tricked up by the stalwart columbo   with that said this is still <num> of the most entertaining in the show 's history benefiting tremendously by the work of the late jack cassidy and star peter falk   besides the notability of being directed by a young steven spielberg the episode also has a air of the macabre because of the future of <num> of its stars cassidy and barbara colby the <num> share several scenes together and it is poignant that both would die tragically within a decade of this filming cassidy in an apartment fire and colby at the hands of assailants yet to be found after over <num> decades   now both demises are true life mysteries 

i was stunned by this film i have been renting antonioni 's films rediscovering them and this film showed me the climax and fruits of his <num> years of directing what an eye for setting color and detail i have never seen such visual beauty and poetry filmed before i had to stop after the <num> story and hold back the tears yes beauty moves me like it moved keats to write ode on a grecian urn this movie is made for the mature emotionally and intellectually audience those hoping to see physical action and soap opera will be disappointed i will have to see this film several times before i can truly appreciate it and judge it this film should be required viewing for all cinematographers and directors   possibly a truly great film on the order of kurosawa 's dreams 

