this is <num> of the few films where i consider the film rendition to be an improvement on the original book the story is clear accessible amusing and interesting and the musical numbers are without a doubt exceptional i adored the cyclical rendition of the old home guard and the charming portobello road a great combination of early animation + real actors techniques which though dated do not detract from the charm of the piece the background of the <num> world war worked well and was not omitted as the film got under way which so often happens in evacuee stories   an often far too underrated film it produces no end to enjoyment for people of all ages the performances from the actors are exceptionally well done and the entire text is neatly tied together and well designed guaranteed to put a smile on your face 

