mockumentaries are proliferating lately so much that the approach therefore needs an injection of fresh and creative material each time it 's used to maintain its vitality this film does not deliver anything but worn out retreads of similar stories an aimless script weak ad libs uninspired acting and unfunny self gratifying humor    the premise would seem promising enough the legend of the loch ness monster is made to order for <num> of these goofy mockumentary misadventures with a vast array of history and legend waiting to be tapped for outrageous satire the film makers totally waste this enormous potential however we get some fool inserting a fake nessie into the water gee that 's original another scene has <num> obnoxious idiot threatening another obnoxious idiot with a gun sidesplitting some gratuitous shots of a pretty girl in a bikini annette did that <num> years ago and far better by the way throughout the movie somebody always seems to be yelling i suppose this is designed to wake up the audience who have nodded off by this point   worst of all though is the relentless salvo of those reality show type interview comments made by the characters not only do they nuke you with this tired joke every <num> seconds but apparently the actors also improvised that 's the only explanation for how humorless the jokes are if lines like i 've never seen anyone write a book about non evidence were actually scripted then the writer should be shot on sight and fed to nessie   no wonder nessie got violent it obviously saw this movie 

