the <num> of <num> jim thompson adaptations released in <num> the other being the more well known grifters after dark has all of thompson 's hallmarks dangerous women the confidence game and characters that are either not as dim as others suspect them of being or not as harmless   jason patric is superb as a former boxer disqualified from the sport for life due to an incident in the ring director james foley uses raging bull esquire sequences to flesh out the back story and the too little seen rachel ward also delivers a great performance but bruce dern is the film 's secret weapon his sweet talking grifter uncle bud subtly commands each of his scenes   there 's almost no comic relief in this film so watch it prepared to be sucked into the void 

