here is a much lesser known <num> 's sci fi with a little different twist an atomic researchers son is kidnapped and held for a ransom of the the father 's atomic secrets   this is a tightly knit atomic sci fi thriller with great production values and above average acting even from the kid the atomic city actually has a movie feel to it unlike a lot of other <num> 's sci fi of this time which which came off more like an episode of a tv show   the atomic city was also actually nominated for an academy award for best screenplay how many other <num> 's sci fi can tout an academy award nomination   great pacing tight direction and some superb location filming in the real atomic city of los alamos new mexico make this <num> worth hunting down the collectors print in circulation is an above average transfer and makes for a great double feature with the atomic man    recommended 

