make no mistake maureen o'sullivan is easily the most gorgeous jane ever and there will never be <num> more gorgeous she is visually stunning that aside it takes more than a beautiful woman to make a good film this is a great film it not only has the classic tarzan aura but also the feel of the continuing saga we become involved with the <num> white hunters who search for ivory <num> of them in love with jane the other a roguish catalyst whose character may be <num> of the best defined and best examined in movie history.and these characterizations are what make this great action flick stand out as a classic there is the uncomfortable racism which is depicted however the africans are depicted as individuals and at the end <num> even become more heroic than the white hunters and stand out as such in fact the <num> not named evokes probably more sympathy from the audience than any other characters the finale also is <num> of the reasons to enjoy this movie the great lion attack has never been duplicated and the horror is well implied with character reactions more so than a modern gore movie would do with graphic depiction if i left anything out it is because i do not want to soil the picture for those who have n't seen it but it is everything you could want in a movie 

