s in this film the ballet dancers stretching when alex goes for the <num> time to apply for an audition they look so lovely and classy and at least this helps to underline the difference between her current dance career and the <num> she aspires to the other good scene was the break dancing in the street i also liked the ice skater 's parents they were funny   some other random points who was hanna and how did alex get to know her what was an <num> year old doing living in a converted warehouse all alone how did she afford that lovely barre and all the furniture?where were her family was that scene in the nude club really necessary the person who wrote in their comment that it was something like a disney film needs their head examined and anyway what happened to the ice skater    many people said the film was poor but they liked the message do n't give up hope keep on trying and your dreams will come true watch the little mermaid instead 

i saw this film many years ago along with another of shepitko 's films wings as part of a soviet film series at a local film archive but none of shepitko 's films as far as i can tell have ever made it to video or dvd in the united states ascent is a great film by any standard with stunning black and white photography hypnotic direction and actors so deep into their roles that you have no sense of them merely giving a performance although the period details of russian resistance to and collaboration with german occupation are very telling the story is timeless <num> russian partisans are captured by the germans and the interrogation tests their integrity as well as their courage i suspect the reason why it has not been released on dvd by the russians here comes the spoiler is that the jewish intellectual and not the tough russian peasant is the partisan who resists both threats and temptation goes serenely to his death and sets an heroic example for the villagers 

