ok here is how i do this i grade movies on <num> components each component will inherently start with <num> points it can then lose or gain <num> points for a possible <num> or <num>   mood action romance comedy drama suspense i give this component <num> points it had a perfect balance of all <num> aspects the action was fun and exiting the romance was not overdone but still very emotional and moving i laughed hard and long throughout the movie and still i was captivated by the fantastic drama and riveting suspense   plot i give this component <num> points i thought all the good fairy tales had already been told i found my self sitting in the theatre returned to my childhood and in that instant i again believed in unicorns wicked witches and falling stars that make dreams come true   cinema photography i give this component <num> points while the movie captured the story very well in the majority of the angles i found my self more than once trying to figure out what happened just off camera   fx i give this component <num> points i love that they used c.g.i sparingly the epic scenes were believable the magical powers were frighteningly realistic all in all less is more and this had it all cast i give this component <num> points no names and seasoned actors alike the cast was amazing michelle pfeiffer was wonderfully wicked charlie cox made tristan come to life claire danes gave emotion to the stars and i will never look and robert de niro the same again   acting i give this component <num> points even the newbie actors played their rolls to perfection once again i will never look and robert de niro the same again   character development i give this component <num> points this felt a little rushed and i think if the movie had been a bit longer they could have done the characters a little better justice   dialogue i give this component <num> points the dialogue was smart witty fun   even the mush had good dialogue   score i give this component <num> points i can honestly remember only <num> small piece of music from the entire movie i am not complaining beyond the fact that the music could be more memorable   ending i give this component <num> points almost perfect ending i feel that certain aspects of the ending should have been more pronounced while others could have been more subdued but no threads were left untied   total <num> buy the dvd hel yes see it in the theatre most definitely bottom line excellent movie for everyone epic i strongly recommend seeing it in the theatre i know i 'll be going back for seconds 

